Fix the BLOCKING findings of the Codex review ops/codex/review-20261105T175251.md (read it in full) in bin/memguard and eval/tests/test_memguard.py. Constraints are dec 021 item 1 (ops/decisions/021-owner-oom-hardening-2026-11-05.md). Python stdlib only, /usr/bin/env python3 (3.12), unprivileged. Do NOT touch bin/job (owner-protected) or anything outside bin/memguard and eval/tests/test_memguard.py, apart from new test helper files under eval/tests/.

Required changes:
1. Allowlist on EVERY signal recipient. A descendant of a marked root is killed only if it is itself eligible: our uid, and (GEMMA_JOB_CAP in its own environ, which is inherited, OR the cwd+RSS>3G rule), and not a claude/node/codex/tmux/Claude-session process. That includes the final root.
2. Identity-bound actions. Record (pid, starttime from /proc/<pid>/stat field 22) at classification. Before every signal or oom_score_adj write, re-read starttime and skip on mismatch. Prefer os.pidfd_open + signal.pidfd_send_signal where available (opening the pidfd, then re-checking starttime, closes the race), falling back to os.kill with the starttime check.
3. Membership completeness. A job's members are all eligible processes carrying the marker of the SAME bin/job wrapper. Do not rely on current ancestry alone; include marked orphans (reparented to init/subreaper). Do repeated discovery passes during the kill (re-scan until two consecutive scans find no live eligible member, at most ~5 s), rescan after the root grace period, and compute survivors from an independent final inventory of all eligible members, not only those signalled. To associate orphans with a job without an extra env var: group marked processes by the GEMMA_JOB_CAP marker value plus the wrapper pid/pgid recorded in ops/jobs/*.status ("running <pid> <start> <pgid>"; old 3-field lines have no pgid). A marked process whose process group matches a running job's pgid belongs to that job. Marked orphans in no running job's pgid form an "orphan" job and are still eligible.
4. /proc access contract: read only /proc/<pid>/{environ,cwd,status,stat}. Remove the cmdline read. Derive job_name from ops/jobs/*.status: the line whose pid or pgid matches the root, the root's pgid or its process group.
5. The bin/send mail call gets timeout=10 and a check of its exit status (log failures). It must never stall the poll loop.
6. Tests: (a) the dummy non-target must NOT carry GEMMA_JOB_CAP (strip it from the env), and its oom_score_adj assertion compares against the baseline it inherited, not 0. (b) The survivor check re-inventories all processes with the test job's marker after the kill. (c) Cleanup rediscovers descendants before killing parents. (d) Add deterministic unit tests on MOCKED snapshots (no real allocation) for: an unmarked small child of a marked parent is NOT signalled; pid reuse (starttime changed) is NOT signalled; a marked orphan is found and killed; a fork during the kill is caught by the rescan; survivors are computed from the final inventory. Keep the real-allocation test at <=3G total and runnable under bin/job.
Acceptance: `python3 -m pytest eval/tests/test_memguard.py -q` passes (the real-allocation test may be marked so it runs only when MEMGUARD_LIVE=1; report both modes if the sandbox permits). bin/memguard --dry-run for one pass against the live system prints its targets without signalling. List any finding you did not fix, with the reason.
