1. Membership: when GEMMA_JOB_ID is present in a process's environ, use it as the PRIMARY job grouping key (exact fixed-string compare), so setsid'ed or reparented members stay in their job. Keep the existing eligibility allowlist. For legacy jobs without GEMMA_JOB_ID, preserve known (pid, starttime) members across PGID/ancestry changes. The final survivor inventory must use the same membership. Regression tests (mocked): a discovered child calls setsid (PGID changes) -> still killed, survivors correct; a legacy 3-field job's child is reparented -> still tracked.
2. Revalidate eligibility immediately before every action (signal and oom_score_adj write), not just identity: uid, session-process exclusion (comm in the claude/node/codex/tmux set, or a shell of a Claude session), and marker-or-cwd/RSS eligibility, re-read after the pidfd is opened (exec keeps starttime). Regression test (mocked): a process whose comm changes to node between classification and signal is NOT signalled; the same for an oom_score_adj write.
